# EDS-007 – ITIL Mapping

**Document ID:** EDS-007
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Approved
**Owner:** Enterprise Runbooks Project
**Last Updated:** 2026-08-06

---

# 1. Purpose

The ITIL Mapping Standard describes how the Enterprise Documentation Framework supports selected ITIL 4 Management Practices.

This document is not intended to replace the official ITIL 4 guidance. Instead, it demonstrates how the documentation standards and operational runbooks within this repository contribute to consistent IT service management.

---

# 2. Scope

This standard applies to the entire Enterprise Runbooks repository, including:

* Framework documents (EDF)
* Documentation Standards (EDS)
* Templates (TMP)
* Operational Runbooks (RB)

---

# 3. Mapping Philosophy

The repository is designed to support operational excellence by providing standardized, repeatable, and maintainable documentation.

Each document contributes to one or more ITIL 4 Management Practices.

---

# 4. ITIL Practice Mapping

| ITIL 4 Practice                  | Repository Contribution                                                                   |
| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Incident Management              | Standardized runbooks reduce recovery time and improve operational consistency.           |
| Problem Management               | Documented procedures support root cause analysis and long-term improvements.             |
| Change Enablement                | Templates and standardized documentation improve change planning and execution.           |
| Monitoring and Event Management  | Operational runbooks define validation and health check procedures.                       |
| Service Configuration Management | Documentation reflects standardized operational configurations and procedures.            |
| Availability Management          | Runbooks support planned maintenance and rapid service restoration.                       |
| Information Security Management  | Documentation standards promote secure handling of operational information.               |
| Knowledge Management             | The repository provides a structured and reusable operational knowledge base.             |
| Continual Improvement            | Versioning, reviews, and lifecycle management support ongoing documentation improvements. |

---

# 5. Enterprise Documentation Mapping

The documentation hierarchy supports ITIL practices as follows.

| Document Type | Primary ITIL Contribution |
| ------------- | ------------------------- |
| EDF           | Governance                |
| EDS           | Standardization           |
| TMP           | Process consistency       |
| RB            | Operational execution     |

Each layer contributes to a consistent documentation ecosystem aligned with ITIL principles.

---

# 6. Operational Benefits

Applying this documentation framework provides several operational benefits.

* Improved documentation consistency
* Reduced operational risk
* Faster onboarding of new team members
* Better audit readiness
* Improved knowledge sharing
* Increased repeatability of operational tasks
* Support for continual service improvement

---

# 7. Limitations

This repository supports ITIL practices through documentation standards and operational guidance.

It does not implement ITIL processes, organizational structures, service management tools, or governance models.

Organizations should adapt the documentation to their own IT Service Management framework.

